  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public boolean isMatch(String s, String p) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return false;\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "Look at the first character match, and whether the next pattern character is a `*`.",
    "With a star, either skip `x*` entirely, or (if the first character matches) consume one character of `s` and keep the star.",
    "def match(i, j):\n    if j == len(p): return i == len(s)\n    first = i < len(s) and p[j] in (s[i], '.')\n    if j + 1 < len(p) and p[j+1] == '*':\n        return match(i, j + 2) or (first and match(i + 1, j))\n    return first and match(i + 1, j + 1)",
    "Memoizing on (i, j) makes it O(n m). Without memoization the recursion is exponential."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n m)",
    "space": "O(n m)"
  },
